Rune UI Licence

Copyright (c) 2026 tinker-n-tailor. All rights reserved.

Rune UI is free to use. Its code is open to read. You may change it and
send your change to the author. You may not share it or publish a changed
version without the written permission of the author.

You may:

- download, install and use Rune UI to play the game, at no cost;
- read the code to learn how it works;
- change your own copy for your own use;
- fork the code on GitHub, to send a change to the author, and keep the
  fork until your pull request is closed.

You may not, without the written permission of the author:

- upload Rune UI, or a changed version of it, to any site or service. The
  one exception is a fork on GitHub that you keep only to send a pull
  request;
- put Rune UI, or a part of it (code or pictures), into another mod, a
  mod pack or any other work;
- sell Rune UI, or ask for money for it or for access to it.

To send a change:

1. Fork the code on GitHub and make your change.
2. Open a pull request. The author reads it and decides.
3. If the author accepts, the change becomes a part of Rune UI.

You keep the copyright of your part. You give the author a permanent and free
right to use it, change it and publish it as a part of Rune UI. You cannot
take this right back. The right holds under this licence and under any
later licence that the author chooses for Rune UI.

The author names you in the README. The commit lists you as co-author.

A change that the author accepts into version 1.9 or later is under these
rules.

If you send a fix or an idea in another way, you give the author the same
right.

Your fork is only for the pull request. You must delete it when the pull
request is closed. You may not share your fork, or a copy of it, as
a mod or for others to download. You may not tell players to use it.

To ask for permission, write to the author on the page of the mod. The
author is Filchie on CurseForge and TinkernTailor on Nexus Mods:

- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/runescape-dragonwilds/ue4ss-mods/rune-ui
- Nexus Mods: https://www.nexusmods.com/runescapedragonwilds/mods/646

These two pages are the only places where the author publishes the mod
for download. The author also keeps the code on GitHub. A copy of the code
there gives you no right beyond this licence.

Versions 1.0 to 1.6 of Rune UI were released under the MIT licence. The
MIT licence still applies to those versions. Version 1.7 stays under the
earlier text of this licence. This text applies from version 1.9.

